    "raw": "Write `onboardctl`, a sibling binary to `manage`, for synchronous onboard debugging that bypasses the DMZ.\n\n## Execution decision\n\n**Single WorkItem stream on this branch -- no parallel subtodos.**\n\nReason (todos + frequentcommits): one coherent CLI package under `thermo/onboard/onboardctl`; later steps share skeleton, zonespec, and HTTP transport. Parallel child branches would thrash the same files. A lesser agent works head-first sequential chunks; each item has its own step AC. Escalate to a subtodo only if a later item proves to need an independent research branch (unlikely).\n\n## Shape\n\n```text\nonboardctl <subcommand> <zonespec> [extraargs...]\n```\n\nModel after other thermo CLIs: ABC + subclasses that each package their own argparse / help / undo hints. Launcher + `venv-run` `.py` like `manage`.\n\nHome: `thermo/onboard/onboardctl/` (sibling *role* to `thermo/dmz/manage`; talks to boards, not DMZ).\n\n## zonespec (default kind = zone)\n\n| Form | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `zone:xxx` or bare `xxx` | Zone name (kitchen, office, ...). |\n| `hardware:xxx` | Fuzzy hardware type (pico2w / pizero / esp32). `esp32` matches every esp32*; `esp32s3` is narrower. |\n| `dialect:xxx` | IR/protocol (midea, daikin, ...). |\n| `type:xxx` | Device class (ac, heatpump, heat, led, ...). |\n\nResolve via existing zone.env / deployment config. Multi-match: list targets; require narrowing for mutating commands.\n\n## Subcommands (logical actions)\n\nEach prints undo recipe or \"read-only / no undo\".\n\n- `logs`, `version`, `deviceinfo` (read-only)\n- `sendcommand` with defaults (`--mode=cool --fan=auto --state=on --temp=22c` style); bare sendcommand must do something useful and print undo\n- `setvar` (`--debug=bool`, `--verbose=0..4`)\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNo DMZ/`manage` routing for these sync paths. No second zone inventory format."
  },
